ml#Lean.AttributeKind\">AttributeKind</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">validate</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></span> := <span class=\"fn\">fun (<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a>) =&gt; <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Pure.pure\">pure</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit.unit\">(</a><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit.unit\">)</a></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Adds a declaration to the given `Sym.Simp` theorem extension.\nWhen `declName` is a proposition, it is added as a rewrite theorem.\nWhen it is a definition, its equational theorems are added, and its unfolding theorem as a\nfallback. See `getSimpTheoremNames`.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Simp/Attr.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Simp.addSymSimpDecl","kind":"def","line":19,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Simp.addSymSimpDecl","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Simp/Attr.lean#L19-L33"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Simp/Attr.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Simp.addSymSimpTheorem\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Simp</span>.<span class=\"name\">addSymSimpTheorem</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">ext</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Simp/Theorems.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Simp.SymSimpExtension\">SymSimpExtension</a>